      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "V. \u0003Executive summary",
      "pageStart": 13,
      "pageEnd": 16,
      "target": "../sections/sec-003-v-executive-summary.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Audience\nThe primary audience for this guideline is national HIV programme managers, people living \nwith HIV, health-care providers and policy-makers in low- and middle-income countries. This \nguideline update will be a useful resource for clinicians and should help to shape the priorities \nof policy-makers in development agencies, international organizations, nongovernmental \norganizations and other implementing partners. This guideline will also be of value to people \nliving with HIV, communities and civil society organizations to ensure they are informed of the \nupdated guidance and to help",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The executive summary identifies the audience as national HIV programme managers, people living with HIV, health-care providers and policy-makers in low- and middle-income countries. It explains that the update followed WHO Guidelines Review Committee procedures and the GRADE approach. It sets out the public health rationale and introduces a summary table of the new recommendations, the revised monitoring algorithm and clinical considerations for rapid ART initiation.",
