      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "\u0003Methods for developing the guidelines",
      "pageStart": 19,
      "pageEnd": 20,
      "target": "../sections/sec-009-15-methods-for-developing-the-guidelines.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "This publication is linked to the 2016 WHO consolidated guidelines (4) and to previous \nguidelines developed in 2017, 2018 and 2019. These are collectively being compiled into a \nsingle consolidated publication containing all relevant guidance.\nAnnex 1 details the full methods for developing this guideline. In summary, this guideline \nupdate was developed in accordance with procedures established by the WHO Guidelines \nReview Committee (13). The recommendations in the guidelines are based on the GRADE \n(Grading of Recommendations Assessment, Development and Evaluation) approach to \nreviewing e",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Summarises the methods used to develop the guideline, which links to earlier WHO HIV guidelines and followed Guidelines Review Committee procedures and GRADE. It describes how declarations of interest were managed and how systematic reviews and evidence-to-decision tables informed the recommendations.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
