      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "\u0003The dapivirine vaginal ring",
      "pageStart": 21,
      "pageEnd": 22,
      "target": "../sections/sec-012-21-the-dapivirine-vaginal-ring.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Recommendation\nThe dapivirine vaginal ring may be offered as an additional prevention choice for women \nat substantial riska of HIV infection as part of combination prevention approaches.\n(conditional recommendation; moderate-certainty evidence)\na. \t \u0007Substantial risk of HIV infection is defined as HIV incidence greater than 3 per 100 person–years in the absence \nof PrEP (see Box 1).\nBackground\nPrEP (pre-exposure prophylaxis) is the use of ARV drugs by HIV-negative individuals to reduce \nthe acquisition of HIV infection. The results from randomized trials and subsequent open-\nlabel extension s",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Presents the conditional recommendation that the dapivirine vaginal ring may be offered as an extra prevention choice for women at substantial HIV risk. It gives background on oral PrEP uptake since 2015 and describes the ring as a female-initiated silicone device releasing an NNRTI, and it notes that long-acting injectable cabotegravir was not yet assessed.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
